# GraphQL API Development Rules

## Core Principles

- **Schema-First Development**: Define GraphQL schema before implementing resolvers
- **Type Safety**: Use GraphQL Code Generator for TypeScript types
- **Performance**: Implement DataLoader for N+1 query prevention
- **Security**: Use GraphQL depth limiting and query complexity analysis

## Schema Design Rules

- **Naming Conventions**: Use PascalCase for types, camelCase for fields
- **Descriptions**: Always include descriptions for types, fields, and arguments
- **Deprecation**: Use @deprecated directive for deprecated fields
- **Input Types**: Separate input types from output types

```graphql
type User {
  id: ID!
  email: String!
  firstName: String!
  lastName: String!
  profile: UserProfile
  lessons: [Lesson!]!
  createdAt: DateTime!
  updatedAt: DateTime!
}

input CreateUserInput {
  email: String!
  password: String!
  firstName: String!
  lastName: String!
}

input UpdateUserInput {
  firstName: String
  lastName: String
  profile: UpdateUserProfileInput
}
```

## Resolver Implementation Rules

- **Single Responsibility**: Each resolver should handle one specific operation
- **Dependency Injection**: Use NestJS DI container for all dependencies
- **Error Handling**: Use GraphQL errors with proper error codes
- **Validation**: Validate inputs using class-validator decorators

```typescript
@Resolver(() => User)
export class UsersResolver {
  constructor(
    private readonly usersService: UsersService,
    private readonly lessonsService: LessonsService
  ) {}

  @Query(() => [User])
  @UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
  async users(): Promise<User[]> {
    return this.usersService.findAll();
  }

  @Query(() => User)
  @UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
  async user(@Args('id') id: string): Promise<User> {
    const user = await this.usersService.findById(id);
    if (!user) {
      throw new NotFoundException(`User with ID ${id} not found`);
    }
    return user;
  }

  @ResolveField(() => [Lesson])
  async lessons(@Parent() user: User): Promise<Lesson[]> {
    return this.lessonsService.findByUserId(user.id);
  }
}
```

## DataLoader Implementation

- **Batch Loading**: Implement DataLoader for efficient data fetching
- **Caching**: Use DataLoader's built-in caching for request-scoped data
- **Error Handling**: Handle errors gracefully in DataLoader functions

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class UsersDataLoader {
  constructor(private readonly usersService: UsersService) {}

  private batchUsers = new DataLoader(async (userIds: string[]) => {
    const users = await this.usersService.findByIds(userIds);
    const userMap = new Map(users.map((user) => [user.id, user]));
    return userIds.map((id) => userMap.get(id) || null);
  });

  async load(userId: string): Promise<User | null> {
    return this.batchUsers.load(userId);
  }

  async loadMany(userIds: string[]): Promise<(User | null)[]> {
    return this.batchUsers.loadMany(userIds);
  }
}
```

## Subscription Rules

- **Real-time Updates**: Use GraphQL subscriptions for live data updates
- **Authentication**: Secure subscriptions with proper authentication
- **Filtering**: Implement subscription filtering to avoid unnecessary updates
- **Performance**: Use Redis pub/sub for scalable subscriptions

```typescript
@Resolver(() => Lesson)
export class LessonsSubscriptionResolver {
  @Subscription(() => Lesson, {
    filter: (payload, variables, context) => {
      return payload.lesson.userId === context.user.id;
    },
  })
  lessonUpdated(@Args('userId') userId: string, @CurrentUser() user: User) {
    return pubSub.asyncIterator(`LESSON_UPDATED_${userId}`);
  }
}
```

## Input Validation & Sanitization

- **DTO Classes**: Use class-validator decorators for input validation
- **Custom Validators**: Implement custom validators for complex business rules
- **Sanitization**: Sanitize inputs to prevent injection attacks
- **Type Conversion**: Use class-transformer for automatic type conversion

```typescript
export class CreateLessonInput {
  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  @Length(1, 100)
  title: string;

  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  @Length(10, 1000)
  description: string;

  @IsEnum(LessonDifficulty)
  difficulty: LessonDifficulty;

  @IsArray()
  @ValidateNested({ each: true })
  @Type(() => CreateExerciseInput)
  exercises: CreateExerciseInput[];
}
```

## Error Handling

- **GraphQL Errors**: Use proper GraphQL error types and codes
- **Custom Errors**: Implement custom error classes for business logic errors
- **Error Filtering**: Use exception filters to transform errors appropriately
- **Logging**: Log errors with proper context for debugging

```typescript
export class LessonNotFoundException extends GraphQLError {
  constructor(lessonId: string) {
    super(`Lesson with ID ${lessonId} not found`, {
      extensions: {
        code: 'LESSON_NOT_FOUND',
        lessonId,
        http: { status: 404 },
      },
    });
  }
}

@Catch(LessonNotFoundException)
export class LessonNotFoundExceptionFilter implements GqlExceptionFilter {
  catch(exception: LessonNotFoundException, host: ArgumentsHost) {
    const gqlHost = GqlArgumentsHost.create(host);
    const context = gqlHost.getContext();

    // Log the error
    context.logger.error(`Lesson not found: ${exception.message}`, {
      lessonId: exception.extensions?.lessonId,
      userId: context.user?.id,
    });

    return exception;
  }
}
```

## Performance Optimization

- **Query Complexity**: Implement query complexity analysis
- **Depth Limiting**: Limit GraphQL query depth to prevent abuse
- **Caching**: Use Redis caching for frequently accessed data
- **Pagination**: Implement cursor-based pagination for large datasets

```typescript
@Module({
  imports: [
    GraphQLModule.forRoot<ApolloDriverConfig>({
      driver: ApolloDriver,
      autoSchemaFile: join(process.cwd(), 'src/schema.gql'),
      playground: process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production',
      introspection: process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production',
      plugins: [
        require('graphql-depth-limit')(7),
        require('graphql-query-complexity')({
          estimators: [
            fieldExtensionsEstimator(),
            simpleEstimator({ defaultComplexity: 1 }),
          ],
          maximumComplexity: 1000,
        }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
})
export class GraphQLAppModule {}
```

## Testing Rules

- **Resolver Testing**: Test all resolvers with proper mocking
- **Schema Testing**: Validate GraphQL schema integrity
- **Integration Testing**: Test GraphQL endpoints end-to-end
- **Performance Testing**: Test query performance and complexity

```typescript
describe('UsersResolver', () => {
  let resolver: UsersResolver;
  let usersService: UsersService;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const module: TestingModule = await Test.createTestingModule({
      providers: [
        UsersResolver,
        {
          provide: UsersService,
          useFactory: () => ({
            findAll: jest.fn(),
            findById: jest.fn(),
          }),
        },
      ],
    }).compile();

    resolver = module.get<UsersResolver>(UsersResolver);
    usersService = module.get<UsersService>(UsersService);
  });

  it('should return an array of users', async () => {
    const result = [{ id: '1', email: 'test@example.com' }];
    jest.spyOn(usersService, 'findAll').mockResolvedValue(result);

    expect(await resolver.users()).toBe(result);
  });
});
```

## Security Considerations

- **Authentication**: Implement JWT-based authentication for all protected operations
- **Authorization**: Use role-based access control for field-level permissions
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limiting for GraphQL operations
- **Query Analysis**: Monitor and analyze GraphQL queries for suspicious patterns
